Verbatim copies of example/*.yml from github.com/immortal/immortal
(v0.24.7, commit 35afc96), the configurations its author ships as
documentation.

They are here as fuzz seeds and as a conversion smoke test, because
synthesized input missed what these caught at once: every one of them
uses a bare command (`cmd: sleep 30`), immortal resolves it through
PATH, slinit does not, and the conversion was emitting services that
could not start. A hand-written seed corpus had no reason to look like
that; the upstream's own examples did.

Licence: immortal is MIT (see the upstream repository). Kept verbatim so
a diff against a newer upstream is meaningful.
